// spec: a reference bound to an object of another scalar type outside a call's arguments is an error, as in C++: a range-for's non-const loop variable (`for (double& d : ints)`), a reference member given another type (a const one too: its temporary would die with the constructor, [class.base.init] 8), a function's reference result returning another type (its temporary would die with the return), and a local rvalue reference given an lvalue of its type (language/rvalue_reference_given_lvalue_is_error for a parameter)
// found by thread B (2026-11-05): kpp bound the other type's bytes (`double& r` over an int wrote 8 bytes into 4: the program crashed) and `S&& r = a;` bound a itself, so a move from r emptied a
// error: reference_of_other_type_bound_outside_call_is_error.kpp:22: error: the loop variable of type double& over elements of type int32: a non-const lvalue reference binds only an element of its type
// error: reference_of_other_type_bound_outside_call_is_error.kpp:11: error: the reference member of type const double& given a value of type int32: a reference member binds only an object of its type
// error: reference_of_other_type_bound_outside_call_is_error.kpp:13: error: a function returning const double& returns a value of type int32: a reference result refers only to an object of its type
// error: reference_of_other_type_bound_outside_call_is_error.kpp:30: error: the S&& variable given an lvalue of its type: an rvalue reference binds only a temporary or what move() gives, never the object itself
class A
{
public:
  const double& r;
  A(const int& i) : r(i) {}
};
const double& widen(const int& i) { return i; }
class S
{
public:
  std::String s;
};
double loop()
{
  int arr[2] = {1, 2};
  for (double& d : arr)
    d = 0.5;
  return arr[0];
}
std::String bind()
{
  S a;
  a.s = "hi";
  S&& r = a;
  S b = std::move(r);
  return a.s;
}
int main()
{
  int i = 7;
  A a(i);
  std::println(loop(), " ", a.r, " ", widen(i), " [", bind(), "]");
  return 0;
}
